# Nothing but source belongs here. The builds this tool reads and the reports
# it writes are both reproducible from the tool plus the archives, and both are
# far too large to keep.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- inputs
#
# The builds being analysed: 150-200MB each, somebody else's release artefacts,
# every one of them re-downloadable. `apkdiff.sh --intake` files them as
# <versionCode>.apk / .aab; the underscore and stray-name forms are how they
# arrive before that. builds/ is only a convention — the tool takes a build
# from anywhere and searches the directory the file is already in — but keeping
# them in one place is what stops a gigabyte of archives sitting in the source
# root, so the directory is ignored whole as well as by extension.
builds/
*.apk
*.apk_
*.aab
*.aab_
*.apks
*.xapk

# Payloads pulled out of a build. These land under a run directory, but a
# stray one in the working directory is the same mistake with less warning.
*.dex
*.so

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- outputs
#
# Analysis runs. A single pair extracts hundreds of megabytes of dex and .so
# into work/, so this must never be committed; the reports beside it are
# regenerated by re-running the tool. runs/ is where apkdiff.sh writes unless
# told otherwise; apkdiff-* is what an explicit -o name usually looks like.
runs/
apkdiff-*/
out/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- build
#
# rust/target is ignored from here rather than from a second .gitignore inside
# rust/: one file to read is the whole point of this one.
rust/target/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- test
#
# .venv is the interpreter run-tests.sh prefers; coverage/ is bashcov's HTML
# report, htmlcov/ is coverage.py's, and .coverage.* are the per-process data
# files the parallel runs leave for `coverage combine` to merge.
.venv/
.pytest_cache/
coverage/
htmlcov/
.coverage
.coverage.*
lcov.info

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- editors, OS
.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*.orig
*.rej

# Release notes are written per app analysed and kept out of the repo.
docs/
